✅ Thunk vs Saga ?
Thunk → Middleware that lets you write action creators returning 
functions instead of objects, mainly for simple async logic (e.g., API calls).

Saga → Middleware using generator functions for more complex 
async workflows, handling side effects in a more testable and controllable way.


